BipedalWalker is a 2D bipedal locomotion environment where a two-legged robot must walk forward across rough terrain without falling. The robot has two legs, each with a hip and knee joint, and the goal is to move as far right as possible without falling.
The state is a vector of 24 elements, representing the following:
- state[0]: hull angle speed (-inf to inf)
- state[1]: angular velocity (-inf to inf)
- state[2]: horizontal velocity (-1 to 1, scaled)
- state[3]: vertical velocity (-1 to 1, scaled)
- state[4]: position of joint 0 (hip 1) (-inf to inf)
- state[5]: angular speed of joint 0 (-inf to inf)
- state[6]: leg 1 ground contact (0 or 1)
- state[7]: position of joint 1 (knee 1) (-inf to inf)
- state[8]: angular speed of joint 1 (-inf to inf)
- state[9]: leg 1 lower ground contact (0 or 1)
- state[10]: position of joint 2 (hip 2) (-inf to inf)
- state[11]: angular speed of joint 2 (-inf to inf)
- state[12]: leg 2 ground contact (0 or 1)
- state[13]: position of joint 3 (knee 2) (-inf to inf)
- state[14]: angular speed of joint 3 (-inf to inf)
- state[15]: leg 2 lower ground contact (0 or 1)
- state[16-23]: 10 LIDAR rangefinder readings (0 to 1), detecting the terrain ahead
The action space is a vector of 4 float numbers, each in [-1, 1], representing the torques applied to the 4 joints:
- action[0]: torque applied to hip joint 1
- action[1]: torque applied to knee joint 1
- action[2]: torque applied to hip joint 2
- action[3]: torque applied to knee joint 2
The policy is a linear policy with 100 parameters and works as follows:
action = state @ W + b, where
state = [state[0], state[1], ..., state[23]]
W = [[params[0],   params[1],   params[2],   params[3]  ],
    [params[4],   params[5],   params[6],   params[7]  ],
    [params[8],   params[9],   params[10],  params[11] ],
    [params[12],  params[13],  params[14],  params[15] ],
    [params[16],  params[17],  params[18],  params[19] ],
    [params[20],  params[21],  params[22],  params[23] ],
    [params[24],  params[25],  params[26],  params[27] ],
    [params[28],  params[29],  params[30],  params[31] ],
    [params[32],  params[33],  params[34],  params[35] ],
    [params[36],  params[37],  params[38],  params[39] ],
    [params[40],  params[41],  params[42],  params[43] ],
    [params[44],  params[45],  params[46],  params[47] ],
